-Used in various visualization tools and research projects for rendering large-scale volumetric data [S1, unofficial].
+**Origin:**
+GigaVoxels was introduced by Cyril Crassin et al. in 2011 [S2, unofficial]. It is a key component of the rendering technology behind Unreal Engine 4 [S2, unofficial].
+
+**History:**
+The technique was developed to address the limitations of dense voxelization and traditional ray tracing for large scenes. It builds on the concept of sparse voxel octrees and brick-based rendering [S2, unofficial].
+
+**Usage:**
+Used in real-time rendering engines, particularly for large-scale environments and global illumination effects [S2, unofficial].
 
